# LunchLedger AI

## Overview

LunchLedger AI is a voice-first, AI-powered expense management application for friend groups.

Unlike Splitwise, users do not manually create expenses through forms.

Instead, they simply speak or type naturally:

> "Ali and Usman only went today. Ali paid 1200."

The AI understands:

- Intent
- Participants
- Payer
- Amount
- Missing users
- Guest users
- Group context

It then updates the database automatically.

The project should showcase modern AI engineering using LangGraph, tool calling, structured outputs, and deterministic business logic.

---

# Goal

Build a production-quality SaaS application using:

- TypeScript
- Node.js
- Fastify
- LangGraph JS
- LangChain JS
- PostgreSQL
- Prisma
- Next.js
- Tailwind
- shadcn/ui

This is NOT a chatbot.

This is an AI Agent that performs actions using tools.

---

# Product Vision

Imagine five friends who eat lunch together every day.

Every day:

Someone pays.

Participants may change.

Someone new may join.

Someone may not come.

Instead of opening an app and filling forms, one person simply says:

"Ali paid 2500 today.
Usman wasn't with us."

The AI records everything correctly.

---

# Core Features

## Groups

Users can create multiple groups.

Examples:

- Office Friends
- University Friends
- Cricket Team
- Family

Each group has different members.

---

## Members

Groups contain members.

Members can be:

Permanent members

Example

Ali
Ahmed
Hamza
Usman
Faizan

Temporary guests

Example

Bilal joins only today.

Guests should only affect one expense.

---

## Expense Recording

Users should be able to say things naturally.

Examples

Ali paid 2400.

Only Ali and Ahmed went today.

Everyone except Hamza.

Me, Ali and Bilal had lunch.

Ahmed paid for everyone.

Ali paid 1800 for himself and me.

I paid 900 today.

The AI should correctly identify:

payer

participants

amount

group

date

---

## Balance Tracking

The system should maintain running balances.

Example

Ali paid 2500

Participants:

Ali
Ahmed
Hamza
Faizan
Usman

Each share:

500

Balances

Ali +2000

Ahmed -500

Hamza -500

Faizan -500

Usman -500

---

## Settlement

Users can settle debts.

Examples

Ahmed paid Ali 500.

I gave Hamza 700.

After settlement, balances update automatically.

---

## Expense History

Examples

Show today's expenses.

Show last week's lunches.

Show all expenses this month.

---

## Recommendation

The AI can answer:

Who should pay tomorrow?

Who owes me money?

How much do I owe Ali?

Who spent the most this month?

---

# Voice First

The application should eventually support voice.

Pipeline

Voice

↓

Speech-to-text

↓

LangGraph

↓

Database Tools

↓

Response

↓

Text-to-speech

For MVP, text input is sufficient.

Architecture should support voice later.

---

# AI Responsibilities

AI should ONLY

Understand language

Extract entities

Choose tools

Ask clarification questions

Generate responses

AI should NEVER

Calculate balances

Update balances manually

Split expenses

Perform business calculations

Business logic must remain deterministic.

---

# Architecture

AI Layer

↓

Application Services

↓

Database

AI understands.

Services calculate.

Database stores.

---

# LangGraph

Create a graph with these nodes.

User Input

↓

Intent Detection

↓

Entity Extraction

↓

Participant Resolver

↓

Tool Executor

↓

Response Generator

Each node should be independent.

---

# Supported Intents

ADD_EXPENSE

SHOW_BALANCE

SHOW_HISTORY

SETTLE_PAYMENT

WHO_SHOULD_PAY

ADD_MEMBER

CREATE_GROUP

REMOVE_MEMBER

---

# Entity Extraction

Extract

payer

participants

amount

group

date

description

Example

Input

Ali paid 2400.

Only Ali and Ahmed went.

Output

{
  "intent": "ADD_EXPENSE",
  "payer": "Ali",
  "participants": [
    "Ali",
    "Ahmed"
  ],
  "amount": 2400
}

---

# Participant Resolver

Should understand

Everyone

Everyone except Ali

Only Ali and Ahmed

Me

Myself

All of us

Bilal also joined

Temporary guest

Missing members

Unknown names

If a name is unknown:

Ask

"Bilal is not a member.
Would you like to add him temporarily or permanently?"

---

# Tool Layer

Implement LangChain tools.

Examples

createExpense()

calculateBalances()

getBalances()

createSettlement()

getExpenseHistory()

createGroup()

addMember()

removeMember()

getMembers()

These tools call application services.

Never access Prisma directly inside AI nodes.

---

# Business Logic

Expense calculation must NOT use AI.

Example

Expense

2500

Participants

5

Share

500

Payer receives

2000

Others owe

500

Everything must be deterministic.

---

